  "analysis_type": "descriptive",
  "question": "For four paper-named GRCm39 loci, how do paired-library RNA and common-region fragment changes differ in the two GSE329778 contrasts, and how sensitive are they to region, depth weighting and prior RNA-QC selection?",
  "decision": "Execute every eligible fixed Q4a case and retain source/locus/subset holds; describe paired measurements without a regulatory-memory or population inference. Exact author replay and original state-resolved Q4 remain held.",
  "strongest_rival": "Composition, lineage/genotype/sorting selection, sparse counts, processing and annotation-defined region choice can explain nonparallel RNA/fragment patterns without regulatory priming. Mouse/preparation independence and author state maps remain unverified.",
  "discriminator": "Same exact positive-RNA/nuclear-fragment barcode sets for both modalities; compare source-defined TSS-window unions with gene bodies, pooled with equal-barcode summaries, and prior RNA-QC intersection. These distinguish measurement/selection sensitivity, not biological mechanism or cell-state effects.",
  "evidence_refs": [
